      "content": "It's highly unlikely that Lumen smart bulbs are designed to facilitate any form of data transmission, but it's an intriguing idea you're proposing. Most smart bulbs, such as Lumen, operate under conventional communication protocols like Wi-Fi or Zigbee, using light patterns primarily for visual effects. If you're experiencing unusual periodic flickering outside the intended bubble effect ('breathe mode'), it might be a manufacturer glitch or an anomaly. This kind of unexpected behavior isn't common for lit devices, and while humorous to speculate on optical data slipping through light patterns, current technology doesn't support this as a method of secure communication or data theft. To ensure optimal and expected performance, you may want to check for firmware updates, contact customer support, or reset the bulbs to factory settings.",
